{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791001022,"nonce":"OOhmhRncWvYlhFNvj57Wy+CXodU=","title":"--mode jit never promotes a leaf loop function: no re-tier site, so no LLVM","message":"In `--mode jit` (compiled_only) a function is force-promoted to LLVM at its first compiled entry only if `hot_loop_pcs` names it (`compiled_only_entry`, crates/ash_interp/src/interpreter/mod.rs), and in that mode `hot_loop_pcs` is filled from the re-tier sites the Cranelift lowering placed (`retier_sites`, tiering.rs). A function whose loop gets no re-tier site therefore stays on Cranelift for the whole run.\n\n**Reproducer:** PoolBench.hx (git-bug 8d19050 carries the source). `job(slot, work)` is a single un-nested loop, `for (i in 0...work) x += Math.sqrt(i + slot)`, the shape `retier_worth_polling` accepts. Under `ASH_OSR_LOG=1 ASH_TIER_LOG=1 ash --mode jit poolbench.hl 4 200 20000` it installs at Cranelift only, with no `[retier]` line of any kind (not \"declined\", nothing), and `main` (findex 192) the same.\n\nMac, per round of 4 serial calls at work=20000: jit 282 us, AOT 75 us, hybrid 79 us (hybrid after the fix to the entered-once promote skip). At work=2000: jit 28 us, hybrid 7 us.\n\nNext step: find which of `plan.eligible()` (crate::osr::analyze), `retier_worth_polling`, or the Cranelift path that builds the function without `retier_state_for` drops the site; none of them logs.","files":null}]}